  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/adolfos-cory-corydoras-adolfoi",
      "html": "<p>A very cool, uncommon species of corydoras. It has a black line across its back and a black vertical mask in the eye area.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/adolfos-cory-corydoras-adolfoi",
      "html": "<p>Currently kept at a pH of 6-7, but they can adapt to a variety of pH.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/adolfos-cory-corydoras-adolfoi",
      "html": "<p>Currently fed blackworms, frozen bloodworms and pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/adolfos-cory-corydoras-adolfoi",
      "html": "<p>They are very peaceful and suitable for many community tanks. Do not keep them with big fish that may try to eat them, as this will likely result in the death of both fish. They are best kept in groups as they like to school here and there.</p>"
    }
  ],
